    "text": "Right now, almost every barrel of oil on Earth is priced in one currency. Not the currency of the country that pumps it, not the currency of the country that buys it, the U.S. dollar. And that one fact lets America borrow cheaper than almost anyone, cut whole countries off from the world economy, and spend money other nations simply can't. But here's the strange part, it was never written into a treaty. It began with a broken promise, an oil embargo, and a secret deal in the desert. And in twenty twenty four, millions of people believe that deal had just expired. So what really happened?",
